### Did the Indian news website *The Wire* publish any article, video, or social media post prior to October 26, 2020, that explicitly referred to the Hindu deity Goddess Durga as a "sex worker"?
Answer: No, *The Wire* did not itself refer to Goddess Durga as a "sex worker." Instead, a February 2016 article titled "Mahishasura and Minister" merely quoted a speech delivered in Parliament by then-HRD Minister Smriti Irani, who was reading from a pamphlet distributed by JNU student organizers. As *The Wire*'s founding editor Siddharth Varadarajan clarified, the text was "Something @smritiirani read in parliament—and which a story in @thewire_in quoted her saying," which was later shared out of context to falsely claim it was "The Wire's view."

